<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11068"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 3:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Somthing struck me today... <BR> <BR>there was the &#34;three dude&#34; who confessed to have killed the Otero family. &#40;were they in fact BTK &#34;helpers&#34; ? BTK큦 brothers? friends? BTK cultmembers?&#41; <BR> <BR>There was the woman who told PI Goad that in 1986 she knew a man &#40;lived with him&#41; who confessed that he killed Vicki Wergle and also other victims and that he was BTK. <BR> <BR>Goad said the man was to young to be BTK. <BR> <BR>Now, could this man be one of the dudes? <BR> <BR>And could there be 2 other &#34;dude큦&#34;/ &#34;BTK cultmembers&#34; still out there? <BR> <BR>Could Rader be one of the &#34; dude큦&#34; <BR> <BR>Could the real BTK be dead? <BR> <BR>Could the real BTK still be out there? <BR> <BR>I guess this theorie is mostly for those who have detailed knowlege of the case, it will be to complicated to explain to those who are new to the case. <BR> <BR>To those of you who know the details, let me know what you think? <BR> <BR>skov <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
