<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11122"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 12:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The popular theory is that the shrinks will find something in raders upbringing &#40;abuse, probably of a sexual nature&#41; that led him to his life of...whatever. <BR> <BR>This is mere speculation, but, for some reason I like the theory that the older Raders &#40;father, or uncle[s], or even a [fiddle-playing]grandfather&#41; were somewhat degenerate and eventually involved all or some of the present generation of Raders in a killing at some point forcing them into a pact of secrecy regarding each other.&#40;Susan?&#41; <BR> <BR>People who commit abuse, are usually victims of abuse. Since Dennis and Dean turned out to be abusive, is stands to reason that either one was abused by an uncle or both the fathers were abusive. <BR> <BR>At any rate, with the original crime to hold over their heads, Rader could have demanded assistance if he wanted, from any of his brothers or cousins in the original pact. <BR> <BR>I think Dennis however was the only one to actually enjoy the killing and acted alone most of the time &#40;simply because he wanted to control the crime scene&#41;. <BR> <BR>I think he originally started out trying to put a gang together but phased the others out after the Oteros, when, while he was busy with Josephene, his partner&#40;s&#41; moved JoeII&#39;s body, without telling him.&#40;or something of that nature&#41; <BR> <BR>If you can believe what the police say, the  Oteros were all murdered between 8:15am and 9:00am. That is 12 min 30 sec per person.  <BR> <BR>For him to be acting alone, they would all have had to be completely bound to where they could not interfere with him, but first he would have to have some of them tie the others.  <BR> <BR>Just getting them all tied up and not losing control of the situation would have taken at least 20 minutes. That leaves him only 7 minutes and 30 seconds to enjoy each killing. Then he hung around another 90 minutes?, molesting the bodies, stealing what he came to steal, or cleaning up his tracks. <BR> <BR>I think it was more like: two of them gained entry, subdued Josephine and JoeII, and tied them up. then found Josephine hiding, or found her after JoeI came back, Overpowered and bound JoeI, and then BTK took Josephine back downstairs, or already had her tied up downstairs, to spend time alone with her while the other one or two stayed upstairs with the three other victims. That would explain why Josephene was killed in such a different manner. <BR> <BR>With two or three men stomping around the house there would be more loose ends to clean up also, which would explain why the neighbor didn&#39;t see the car leave until 10:30. Instead of him just leaving, the two or three of them would have to clean up, get their alibis straight and plan their getaways. <BR> <BR>Then after the police caught the &#34;three dude&#34;, which may or may not have been one&#40;some&#41; of the actual criminals, Rader came up with the serial killer angle,claiming responsibility thus letting the others off the hook before they ratted him out, since he figured on continuing anyway &#40;but no more partners which just cramped his style&#41;. He may have kept them involved by having them make  the puzzles up, and write the poems, make drops and drive getaway cars or pick him up, since he doesn&#39;t seem like the poetry type, maybe did his own puzzles, but a second person doing the drops would make good sense. <BR> <BR>I was thinking also that he would need someone to test-drive the puzzles to be sure he didn&#39;t accidently drop a clue that he didn&#39;t want to.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
