<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->People who read these theories should keep in mind that we are not trying to create a new BTK, I personally want to know why so many versions of the same information is floating around, and particularly how much politics and/or economic clout influenced the aspects of the investigation. It&#39;s obvious that the police have not given the public the true facts, which they admit to some extent. Did they have a good reason? If so I can live with that. Were influential people pulling strings, or the authorities &#34;shaping&#34; the facts? If we don&#39;t ask we will never know. <BR> <BR>Apathy breeds impropriety and it is our job to keep our honest officials honest. <BR> <BR>Originally, the Ghostbusters were pushing hard for a BTK duo. 45 minutes is not much time for one person to gain control of, bind, torture, and suffocate/strangle 4 victims. And we know, since the Otero&#39;s car left at 10:30, he/they spent 90 minutes in the house afer the deaths, so there was no apparent hurry. <BR> <BR>JoeII&#39;s body, it has been reported, to has been discovered laying down, or sitting in a chair, hooded with paper bags, or hooded with t-shirt and plastic bags. It depends on who you talk to. <BR> <BR>If some punk robs a liquor store , killing the clerk, and is caught, his name is all over the news immediately. In the course of three days One person is shotgunned in his own home and then four more people killed in their home. As far as I remember no suspects were ever pursued in connection with the former, and in the latter the &#34;three dude&#34; were never named. The police immediately denied that the two incidents were connected. How did they know? <BR> <BR>Although bound at the wrists and ankles before being strangled, the police didn&#39;t believe, at first, that Vicki Wegerle was a BTK victim. He had to tell them. <BR> <BR>The Mayor was quoted as saying that no murders, that BTK has committed, occured after 1994, when Kansas instituted the death penalty. BTK has not killed ANYONE in 11 years? Are they just taking Rader&#39;s word for it? If Wichita has even one unsolved murder of a woman or girl since 1994, then there is a possibility that BTK has killed in the last ten years. Have they decided not to investigate any more, now that they &#34;got their man&#34;?. <BR> <BR>Granted, it&#39;s nearly impossible to find enough factual information to actually answer all of the questions we still have. But by asking the questions, we can put pressure on the authorities to provide more information or address the false or confused issues. We can&#39;t be sure anything will be addressed during or after the trial because I&#39;m thinking with Rader caught, a lot of people who have been postponing retirement will now call it a life.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11216-->
